# Moonscarlet's Chat Scanner

Chat Scanner watches chat for you and alerts you when someone posts something you care about, complete with sounds and clickable, class-colored player names. It also includes a built-in Chat Filter to hide spam and boost services, independent switches for scanning and filtering, and full regex support.

## How I use it
I keep Trade, LFG and World in a separate chat tab, so my main tab stays clean. When I'm looking for a group or an item, I add it to the watch list and get alerted in my main tab only when it shows up. I also add common spam phrases into the Filter tab so trade chat clutter never shows up in any chat window.

## Features
- **Simple in-game window.** Type `/cs` or click the minimap button.
- **Chat Filter.** Block and hide messages matching phrases or patterns from all chat windows.
- **Independent Controls.** Scanning alerts and chat filtering have separate switches. Turn off sound notifications without disabling spam filtering.
- **Regex & Lua Pattern support.** Toggle between Normal words and Regex mode (`\b`, `\w`, `\s`, `\d`).
- **Session Blocked Log.** Click "View Blocked" on the Filter tab (or `/cs log`) to review messages blocked during your session. Click any player name to whisper them directly.
- **Smart keywords.** Match phrases, require multiple words at once, or exclude words you don't want (e.g. find "LFM Molten Core" but skip "gold").
- **Drag to reorder.** Easily drag the `::` handle on any row to change keyword or filter order.
- **Friend and Guild protection.** Option to ensure friends and guild members are never filtered out.
- **Edit anytime.** Change a keyword or filter in place with one click.
- **Choose your chats.** Guild, Say, Yell and channels on by default. Party, Raid, Battleground, Officer and Whispers optional.
- **Ignore list.** Silence specific players in the scanner without affecting your in-game ignore list.
- **Pick your sound.** Choose your alert sound from a list and preview each one. Can play through the Master volume channel even when game sound is muted.
- **Pick your color & chat tab.** Choose your alert text color and the chat tab where alerts are printed.
- **Raid warning & taskbar flash.** Optional screen-center banner and taskbar icon flashing.
- **Clean and saved.** Skips your own messages, NPCs, and duplicate posts. Window is fully resizable and all settings save across sessions.

## Getting started
1. Type `/cs` (or click the minimap button).
2. On the **Keywords** tab, add what you want alerts for.
3. On the **Filter** tab (`/cs f`), add spam phrases you want hidden from chat.
4. Check the **Chats** tab to choose where to listen.
5. Open the **Settings** tab to choose your sound, color, and preferences, then click **Test notification**.

## Keywords & Filters
| Mode | Input | Matches |
|---|---|---|
| Normal | `LFM Molten Core` | messages containing that phrase |
| Normal | `tank,dungeon` (commas) | messages containing **both** words |
| Normal | Contains: `LFM MC` + NOT: `gold,boost` | LFM MC, but skips mentions of gold or boost |
| Regex | `\b\w+e\w+\b` | words with characters surrounding 'e' |
| Regex | `\bboost\b` | the exact word "boost" |

Spaces count exactly as typed, so `" tank "` only matches the whole word "tank".

## Slash commands (optional)
| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `/cs` | Open or close the window |
| `/cs f` or `/cs filter [on\|off]` | Open the Filter tab, or turn chat filtering on/off |
| `/cs log` | Open the blocked messages log |
| `/cs add [text]` | Add a keyword (`_` = space, `\|` = all must match, `-` = exclude) |
| `/cs addregex [pattern]` | Add a regex keyword |
| `/cs del [number]` | Remove a keyword |
| `/cs toggle [number] ...` | Turn keywords on/off (e.g. `/cs toggle 1 2 3`) |
| `/cs edit [number] [string]` | Replace a keyword |
| `/cs list` | Show your keywords, filters, and settings |
| `/cs clear` | Clear all keywords |
| `/cs addplayer [name]` | Ignore a player |
| `/cs delplayer [number]` | Stop ignoring a player |
| `/cs players` | Show ignored players |
| `/cs clearplayers` | Clear the ignore list |
| `/cs enable` / `/cs disable` | Turn scanner alerts on or off |
| `/cs mute` / `/cs master` / `/cs flash` | Toggle sound / play when muted / taskbar flash |
| `/cs help` | Show all commands |